<hr data-start="329" data-end="332" class="">
<h3 data-start="334" data-end="368" class=""><strong data-start="338" data-end="368">1. Polycomputation Defined</strong></h3>
<p data-start="369" data-end="534" class="">Polycomputation refers to the <strong data-start="399" data-end="469">simultaneous or recursive use of multiple computational substrates</strong>, often across different physical or symbolic layers. It entails:</p>
