cal{S}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.7224em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">âˆˆ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right:0.075em;">S</span></span></span></span></span></span><span> to a symbolic representation </span><span class="inline-math"><span contenteditable="false" class="ProseMirror-widget"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ïƒ</mi><mo>âˆˆ</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Î£</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma \in \Sigma</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.5782em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.03588em;">Ïƒ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">âˆˆ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Î£</span></span></span></span></span></span><span>. Recursive application is defined by:
