lication/x-tex">\mathcal{S} \cup \Sigma</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right:0.075em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">âˆª</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Î£</span></span></span></span></span></span><span> and morphisms given by applications of R. Morphism composition captures the hierarchy of symbolic emergence.</span></p><div contenteditable="false"><hr></div><h3><span>Theoretical Contributions</span></h3><ol data-spread="true" start="1"><li><p><span><strong>Constructor Theory Extension</strong></span><span>:</span></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>Constructor â†’ Polyconstructor</span></p></li><li><p><span>Reinterpretation of constructor capability as symbolic potential.</span></p></li></ul></li><li><p><span><strong>Symbolic Bootstrapping</strong></span><span>:</span></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>Recursive R operations result in chains of symbolic complexity.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Critical for explaining language, tool use, and cultural cognition.</span></p></li></ul></li><li><p><span><strong>Risk of Runaway Symbol Chains</strong></span><span>:</span></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>Open-ended symbolic recursion can lead to unstable or incoherent systems.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Models cognitive ossification (e.g., dogma), unbounded AI inference, or sociotechnical debt.</span></p></li></ul></li><li><p><span><strong>Polycompilative Density Function (PCD)</strong></span><span>:</span></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span class="inline-math"><span contenteditable="false" class="ProseMirror-widget"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>PCD</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>Number&nbsp;of&nbsp;unique&nbsp;symbolic&nbsp;reappropriations</mtext><mrow><mtext>mass&nbsp;or&nbsp;energy&nbsp;of&nbsp;substrate&nbsp;</mtext><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{PCD}(x) = \frac{\text{Number of unique symbolic reappropriations}}{\text{mass or energy of substrate } x}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">PCD</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:1.4133em;vertical-align:-0.4811em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height:0.9322em;"><span style="top:-2.655em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height:3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord text mtight"><span class="mord mtight">mass&nbsp;or&nbsp;energy&nbsp;of&nbsp;substrate&nbsp;</span></span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">x</span></span></span></span><span style="top:-3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height:3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width:0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top:-3.4461em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height:3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord text mtight"><span class="mord mtight">Number&nbsp;of&nbsp;unique&nbsp;symbolic&nbsp;reappropriations</span></span></span></span></span><